     <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_SECURITY_SAFE_BROWSING_STANDARD_WHAT_IT_DOES_HEADING" desc="Heading of the Safe Browsing standard protection column describing what it does">
       What it does
     </message>
+  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_ENABLE_GPC" desc="">
+    Global Privacy Control "Sec-GPC"
+  </message>
+  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_ENABLE_GPC_DIALOG_TITLE" desc="">
+    Global Privacy Control "Sec-GPC"
+  </message>
+  <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_ENABLE_GPC_DIALOG_TEXT" desc="">
+    Enables support for Global Privacy Control signals.
+
+Right to opt-out of sale or sharing: You may request that businesses stop selling or sharing your personal information (“opt-out”).
+
+Businesses cannot sell or share your personal information after they receive your opt-out request unless you later authorize them to do so again.
+
+Please note that it only applies to the states of California (under CCPA and CPRA) and Colorado (under CoPA).
+  </message>
     <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_SECURITY_SAFE_BROWSING_STANDARD_WHAT_IT_DOES_CONTENT" desc="Content of the Safe Browsing standard protection column describing what it does">
       Warns you about sites, downloads, and extensions that are known to be dangerous. You can turn off these warnings at any time. If you see a warning for legitimate content, you can <ph name="BEGIN_LINK">&lt;a target="_blank" href="https://safebrowsing.google.com/safebrowsing/report_error/"&gt;</ph>report an error<ph name="END_LINK">&lt;/a&gt;</ph>.
     </message>
